W: 1. When I die, bury me low,
W: Where I can hear the petroleum flow.
W: A sweeter sound, I never did know.
W: The rolling mills of New Jersey.
W:
W: 2. Down in Trenton, there is a bar.
W: The bums, they come from near and from far.
W: They come by truck, they come by car.
W: The lousy bums of New Jersey.
W:
W: 3. Down in Hoboken, there will be
W: Garbage as far as the eye can see.
W: There's garbage for you, there's garbage for me.
W: The garbage dumps of New Jersey.
W:
W: 4. In Elizabeth, you will find
W: Enough dioxin to blow your mind,
W: It will last a very long time,
W: The toxic wastes of New Jersey.
W:
W: 5. When at last, I decided to roam,
W: Far away from my home in Bayonne.
W: I sat down, and wrote this poem.
W: I wrote an ode to New Jersey.
W:
W: 6. When I die, bury me low,
W: Where I can hear the petroleum flow.
W: A sweeter sound, I never did know.
W: The rolling mills of New Jersey.
